821	    /**
822	     * Flags a newly created owner as a possible (soft) duplicate. Reaching this point means the
823	     * owner already cleared {@link #rejectDuplicateIdentity(OwnerFieldsDto)}, so it does not share
824	     * an existing owner's identity key. A member that declared its household via
825	     * {@code sharesHousehold} is a deliberate addition to a known household, not a suspected
826	     * duplicate, so it is never flagged. Otherwise it is a possible duplicate when an existing owner
827	     * shares the Soundex code of its {@code lastName} and its {@code postcode} while carrying a
828	     * different identity key (see {@link #findPossibleDuplicate(Owner)}). When such an owner is
829	     * found, {@code possibleDuplicate} is set {@code true} and {@code possibleDuplicateOf} to the
830	     * matching owner's id; otherwise {@code possibleDuplicate} is set {@code false} and no matching
831	     * id is recorded. An owner without a postcode can share no postcode and is never a possible
832	     * duplicate.
833	     *
834	     * @param owner the owner being created, already carrying its normalized telephone and postcode
835	     * @param ownerFieldsDto the submitted owner fields carrying the {@code sharesHousehold} flag
836	     */
837	    private void applyPossibleDuplicate(Owner owner, OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
838	        owner.setPossibleDuplicate(false);
839	        owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(null);
840	        if (sharesHousehold(ownerFieldsDto)) {
841	            return;
842	        }
843	        findPossibleDuplicate(owner).ifPresent(existing -> {
844	            owner.setPossibleDuplicate(true);
845	            owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(existing.getId());
846	        });
847	    }
848	
849	    /**
850	     * Finds the existing owner, if any, that makes the given newly created owner a possible (soft)
851	     * duplicate: a non-deleted owner whose {@code lastName} shares the new owner's Soundex code (see
852	     * {@link Owner#soundex(String)}) and whose {@code postcode} matches, while carrying a different
853	     * identity key (see {@link Owner#identityKey(String, String, String)}). Requiring a differing
854	     * identity key keeps a hard duplicate — already rejected with 409 by
855	     * {@link #rejectDuplicateIdentity(OwnerFieldsDto)} — from also being flagged as a soft match, so
856	     * the two household members whose telephones differ (hence differing identity keys, but matching
857	     * Soundex and postcode) are exactly the soft matches surfaced here. This is the single definition
858	     * of the soft-duplicate match; {@link #applyPossibleDuplicate(Owner, OwnerFieldsDto)} only records
859	     * the outcome on the owner. An owner without a postcode can share no postcode and matches nothing,
860	     * so {@link java.util.Optional#empty()} is returned.
861	     *
862	     * @param owner the owner being created, already carrying its normalized telephone and postcode
863	     * @return the matching existing owner, or {@link java.util.Optional#empty()} when none matches
864	     */
865	    private java.util.Optional<Owner> findPossibleDuplicate(Owner owner) {
866	        if (owner.getPostcode() == null) {
867	            return java.util.Optional.empty();
868	        }
869	        String soundex = Owner.soundex(owner.getLastName());
870	        String identityKey = owner.getIdentityKey();
871	        return this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
872	            .filter(existing -> !Owner.isDeleted(existing.getDeleted()))
873	            .filter(existing -> !identityKey.equals(existing.getIdentityKey())
874	                && soundex.equals(Owner.soundex(existing.getLastName()))
875	                && owner.getPostcode().equals(existing.getPostcode()))
876	            .findFirst();
877	    }
