733	     * The number of owners a city must already contain before it is flagged as approaching its
734	     * capacity limit. Once a city holds at least this many owners (but is not yet at
735	     * {@link #CITY_OWNER_CAPACITY}), the create and read responses report {@code capacityWarning}
736	     * true for owners in that city.
737	     */
738	    private static final long CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40L;
739	
740	    /**
741	     * Reports whether the given city is approaching its capacity limit, i.e. whether it already
742	     * contains between {@link #CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD} and {@link #CITY_OWNER_CAPACITY}
743	     * minus one owners (40 to 49) inclusive. The count is taken the same way the hard rejection
744	     * counts a city's owners ({@link #countOwnersInCity(String)}). A {@code null} city never warns.
745	     *
