938	    /**
939	     * Validates the national-number length of an already syntactically valid E.164 telephone
940	     * against its country code. When the number carries a country code this application recognizes
941	     * (see {@link Owner#countryCodeOf(String)}) the digits following that code must have exactly the
942	     * length that code admits ({@code '+61'} => 9 national digits, {@code '+1'} => 10, see
943	     * {@link Owner#nationalNumberLength(String)}). When the country code is recognized but the
944	     * national number is the wrong length an {@link InvalidFieldsException} is thrown, which the
945	     * exception advice renders as a 400 response naming the {@code telephone} field. A country code
946	     * that is not recognized carries no per-country length rule and is left to the general
947	     * 8-to-15-digit E.164 check.
