786	     * Returns this owner's fiscal year formatted as {@code 'FY<YY>'}, where YY is the two-digit
787	     * fiscal-year segment carried by the owner's {@code memberId} (see {@link #getMemberId()}), the
788	     * segment immediately following the leading region code. Because the {@code memberId} is the
789	     * unified identity the fiscal year is now read from, this returns {@code null} when the owner has
790	     * no {@code memberId}, so the fiscal year cannot be derived. The two-digit segment is the last two
791	     * digits of the fiscal year (starting 1 July, see {@link #fiscalYearOf(LocalDate)}) the owner's
792	     * business-day-adjusted {@code registrationDate} fell in when the {@code memberId} was assigned,
793	     * e.g. a {@code memberId} of {@code 'NSW26A1B2C3D45'} yields {@code 'FY26'}. This is the single
794	     * definition of an owner's fiscal year.
795	     *
796	     * @return the owner's fiscal year, or {@code null} when it cannot be derived
797	     */
798	    @Transient
799	    public String getFiscalYear() {
800	        if (this.memberId == null) {
801	            return null;
802	        }
803	        String core = this.memberId;
804	        int dash = core.indexOf('-');
805	        if (dash >= 0) {
806	            core = core.substring(0, dash);
807	        }
808	        return "FY" + core.substring(core.length() - 11, core.length() - 9);
809	    }
